---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import ClosingBand from "../components/ClosingBand.astro";
import FramedPhoto from "../components/FramedPhoto.astro";
import photos from "../data/photos.json";
import imgCity from "../assets/photos/about-city.jpg";

const entities = [
  {
    name: "Green Africa (Incorporated Trustees)",
    text: "A registered Nigerian non-profit carrying the community, education, awareness and collection-mobilisation work, and the grant funding attached to it.",
  },
  {
    name: "Amp10 Limited",
    text: "The commercial entity holding trade, export and investment activity.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About Green Africa"
  description="Who we are, how we're structured, and what we're actually trying to build."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About"
    headline="We're building the boring layer."
    subhead="Not a movement. Not an app. The plumbing that lets everything above it be trusted."
  />

  <section class="rule-t">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-10 py-16 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow text-leaf">01 — Why we exist</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
          Unprovable work doesn't attract capital.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/75 lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <p>
          Plastic recovery in Nigeria doesn't fail for lack of effort. It fails because the effort
          can't be proved, and unprovable work doesn't attract capital.
        </p>
        <p>
          Brands can't fund what they can't report. Credit markets can't price what they can't
          verify. Funders can't scale what they can't audit. Meanwhile the collector at the bottom
          of the chain — who is doing the actual environmental work — captures the smallest share
          of value, because they hold the material and not the evidence.
        </p>
        <p class="font-medium text-ink">We decided the evidence was the thing worth building.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="rule-t">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-10 py-16 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow text-leaf">02 — What we chose not to build</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
          Deliberately narrow. Deliberately asset-light.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/75 lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <p>
          We're not trying to become Nigeria's largest aggregator. We're not building pelletising
          capacity. We're not importing machines.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each of those is a capital-heavy business with someone already better at it than us. Our
          position is deliberately narrow and deliberately asset-light: verify at the point of
          recovery, prove it, and let the value of proof flow to the people who earned it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-pine text-paper">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-10 py-16 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow text-leaf-bright">03 — Recognition</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
          First place overall in a 2025 Africa-wide technology hackathon.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-paper/75 lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <p>
          Green Africa won first place overall and a cross-track championship in 2025, competing
          against more than 1,300 submissions from over 13,000 developers. That recognition helped
          fund the deployment now in progress.
        </p>
        <p>
          It's useful validation; it isn't the product. The machines going into the ground and the
          verified recycling records written to Algorand are the product.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="rule-t">
    <div class="container-x py-16 sm:py-20">
      <p class="eyebrow text-leaf">04 — How we're structured</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
        Two entities, kept deliberately separate.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-px border border-ink/10 bg-ink/10 md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          entities.map((entity, index) => (
            <article class="bg-paper p-7 sm:p-9" data-reveal style={`--d:${index * 120}ms`}>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">{entity.name}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70">{entity.text}</p>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
        The separation is intentional. Grant money and trading revenue shouldn't share a bank
        account, and funders are right to ask which one they're funding.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-sand/60">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-10 py-16 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow text-leaf">05 — Where we are</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
          The problem is local, and so is the answer.
        </h2>
        <FramedPhoto
          src={imgCity}
          alt={photos["about-city"].alt}
          credit={`Photo: ${photos["about-city"].photographer} / Pexels`}
          class="mt-8"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/75 lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <p>
          Founded and operating in Nigeria, with offices in Ibadan and operations across Lagos and
          Oyo States. Hardware is fabricated locally. The team is local. The problem is local, and
          so is the answer.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ClosingBand
    headline="Come and see one."
    body="The best version of this conversation happens standing in front of a machine. If you're in Lagos or Ibadan, we'll show you."
  />
</Base>
